  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n        ««  Shadow Hearts  »»                                   [A-1-06]\n____________________________________________________________________________\n\\\\\\\\¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\                              Valuables\u0001                             \\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\_____________________________________________________________________\\\\\\\\\n   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\nListed here are all of the Valuables in the game, in the order that the game\nlists them.\n\n\n.—————————————————————.———————————————————————————————————————————————————————.\n|  Valuable           |  Description (Menu)                                   |\n'—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————'\n|  Decription (Info)                                                          |\n|                                                                             |\n'—————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————'\n\n.—————————————————————.———————————————————————————————————————————————————————.\n|  Talisman           |  Engraved stone, it shows current Malice level        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Talisman                                                                   |\n|  Glowing stone. A memento from father. When hero awakens as a Harmonixer,   |\n|  the light changes from blue to yellow to red and displays current Malice   |\n|  level.                                                                     |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Pendant            |  Cross-shaped pendant from Father Elliot              |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Pendant                                                                    |\n|  This pendant was given by Father Elliot. In the train, it emits a          |\n|  powerful mystical light that rescues our hero.                             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  SluiceGateHandle   |  Rust-covered gear. Used in a sluice gate             |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Sluice Gate Handle                                                         |\n|  Once a part of a sluice gate, it is now completely rusted over. After the  |\n|  locals were killed in a war, the gate was left untended for ages.          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Anti-Cat Powder    |  Smelly Chinese herb infused with catnip              |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Anti-Cat Powder                                                            |\n|  This incredibly foul smelling medicine contains catnip. It smells foul     |\n|  but is a sure cure for cat troubles.                                       |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Torch              |  Bundle of dried twigs. Used as a light source        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Torch                                                                      |\n|  Dried twigs that have been bundled together for easy use. Useful as an     |\n|  outdoor light source.                                                      |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Metal Bowl         |  Foul-smelling bowl once used by a pathologist.       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Metal Bowl                                                                 |\n|  Measuring bowl used by a pathologist in Zhaoyang Village. Bits of putrid,  |\n|  rotten flesh cling to the bottom.                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Jewel              |  The \"Sealing Stone\". Creates mystic barriers.        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Jewel                                                                      |\n|  Called the \"Sealing Stone\", it is a glowing blue gem used as a tool in     |\n|  the art of dark geomancy to create and strengthen barriers.                |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Salt-dried Fish    |  Dried mackerel for the dedicated fish-lover.         |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Salt-dried Fish                                                            |\n|  Salt-dried mackerel. Bred in deep ocean currents, its meat is firm yet     |\n|  tender. A quack oracle ate 5 of them at Sea Turtle Restaurant. Everyone    |\n|  was disgusted.                                                             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Wood Token         |  Ancient token representing \"Wood\".                   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Wood Token                                                                 |\n|  Ancient token displaying one of the 5 Yin and Yang elements, wood. Used    |\n|  in opening mystical seals or barriers.                                     |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Yawang Gate Key    |  Key to \"Yawang Gate\" leading to Kuihai Tower         |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Yawang Gate Key                                                            |\n|  Key to \"Yawang Gate\", the only entrance to Dehuai's fortress, Kuihai       |\n|  Tower. Obtained by Lieutenant Suketani at the cost of many of his          |\n|  followers' lives.                                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Wugui Room Key     |  Creepy key carved from some animal's bone            |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Wugui Room Key                                                             |\n|  Key hand carved from the spine of some oddly shaped animal. What secret    |\n|  could this eerie key be hiding?                                            |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  B. Dragon VP       |  Painting containing the power of the Blue Dragon     |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Blue Dragon Votive Picture                                                 |\n|  Mystic tool with the power of the Blue Dragon, one of the 4 gods of        |\n|  directions. In the hands of a wicked person, it alone could lay waster to  |\n|  an entire nation.                                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  W. Tiger VP        |  Painting containing the power of the White Tiger     |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  White Tiger Votive Picture                                                 |\n|  Mystic tool containing the power of the White Tiger. It has the power to   |\n|  lay waste to an entire nation. Taken from Kuihai Tower 15 years ago by     |\n|  Colonel Hyuga.                                                             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  B. Tortoise VP     |  Painting with the power of the Black Tortoise        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Black Tortoise Votive Picture                                              |\n|  Mystic tool with the power of the Black Tortoise, one of the gods of       |\n|  directions. In the hands of a wicked person, it alone could lay waste to   |\n|  an entire nation.                                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  R. Phoenix VP      |  Painting containing the power of the Red Phoenix     |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Red Phoenix Votive Picture                                                 |\n|  Mystic tool with the power of the Red Phoenix, one of the 4 gods of        |\n|  directions. In the hands of a wicked person, it alone could lay waste to   |\n|  an entire nation.                                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  East Gate Key      |  Key to gate separating Bistritz and forest           |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  East Gate Key                                                              |\n|  Key to Bistritz town gate. If the gate is for protection from animals,     |\n|  why is there a carving of a sun on the gate and garlic on the key?         |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Kid's Room Key     |  Key for entering the orphans' room                   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Kid's Room Key                                                             |\n|  Key found in a rather questionable orphanage. It opens the Orphans' Room   |\n|  (They called it the Key Room. Those jerks.)                                |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Guestroom Key      |  Key to the mansion's guestroom                       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Guestroom Key                                                              |\n|  Pure gold key from Joshua.                                                 |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Heart Key          |  Bizarre key to mental hospital                       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Heart Key                                                                  |\n|  Key to Calios Mental Hospital. More prison than hospital, there is a dark  |\n|  side to its grand history.                                                 |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Club Key           |  Bizarre key to mental hospital                       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Club Key                                                                   |\n|  Key to prison-like mental hospital. It is worn from the hands of the many  |\n|  cruel torturers who held it.                                               |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Diamond Key        |  Bizarre key to mental hospital                       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Diamond Key                                                                |\n|  This key is for the sole purpose of locking unwanted people away from the  |\n|  rest of society in a prison euphemistically called a hospital.             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Spade Key          |  Hospital room key held by Viscount Rausan            |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Spade Key                                                                  |\n|  Key jealously guarded by the hospital director, Viscount Rausan. It seems  |\n|  to have been polished obsessively and is without even a single scratch.    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Bronze Coin        |  Bronze coin from hospital. Oddly scratched.          |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Bronze Coin                                                                |\n|  Bronze coin with a crab spider symbol etched on it. Probably for some      |\n|  purpose other than money. Deeply scratched from use.                       |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Silver Coin        |  Silver coin from hospital with bird symbol           |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Silver Coin                                                                |\n|  Silver coin inscribed with symbol of the magical burn, Lopuros. Ancient    |\n|  and scarred from years of use.                                             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Gold Coin          |  Gold coin from hospital with demonic crest           |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Gold Coin                                                                  |\n|  Ancient gold coin inscribed with a demonic crest. Thick and heavy, it      |\n|  shines out even in a dark hospital room.                                   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Platinum Coin      |  Platinum coin from hospital with dragon symbol       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Platinum Coin                                                              |\n|  Platinum coin inscribed with the symbol of a dragon. It's impossible to    |\n|  tell whether it's new or old and it rings out with a lovely tone when      |\n|  plunked.                                                                   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Dungeon Key        |  Key carved from the bone of some animal.             |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Dungeon Key                                                                |\n|  Apparently a key to some huge door, it is stamped with the image of some   |\n|  god-like entity. Whether good or evil, it is impossible to tell.           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Doyle Letter       |  Letter from Doyle found in Penitence Room            |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Doyle Letter                                                               |\n|  Letter from Father Doyle found in the Penitence Room. Detailed within is   |\n|  a list of various sins that became privy to him in the confessional.       |\n|                                                                             |\n|  NOTE: While you do get to read this during the game, it never actually     |\n|        makes it into your inventory.                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Oath Grail         |  Grail from which Death drank souls                   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Oath Grail                                                                 |\n|  Death drunk on souls, told the Overlord how to beat the Four Masks.        |\n|  \"Grail weakens Gold; Gold, Staff; Staff, Sword; and Sword, Drink. My oath  |\n|  is to the Grail...\"                                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Crank              |  Crank for starting some kind of machine              ||—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Crank                                                                      |\n|  Crank for starting some kind of machine. Judging by the size of the        |\n|  handle, it must be a machine of terrific dimensions.                       |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Storeroom Key      |  Old key found near water-spitting lion               |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Storeroom Key                                                              |\n|  Extremely rusty key that doesn't look as if it has been well looked        |\n|  after.                                                                     |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Slide              |  Discovered at the doll museum. I see something...    |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Slide                                                                      |\n|  Slide found in dollhouse. The upper half of a young girl can be seen       |\n|  faintly. If I only I had a Projector...                                    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Snake Card         |  Card with a picture of a snake. Useful in shops.     |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Snake Card                                                                 |\n|  Card from the Wholesale Items Guild (WIG). Gives various benefits. But if  |\n|  you lose on discount 5 times in a row with insufficient funds, it becomes  |\n|  inactive.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Star Card          |  Guild card from Shanghai with picture of star.       |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Star Card                                                                  |\n|  Card acquired from a fortune-telling boy in Shanghai. Very useful in       |\n|  shops. Don't leave home without it.                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Moon Card          |  Guild card with picture of moon. From Bistritz.      |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Moon Card                                                                  |\n|  Guild card found in Bistritz. This one has a moon picture on it. Those     |\n|  guild folks must be astrology fans.                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Sun Card           |  Guild card with Sun picture. Bought in London        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Sun Card                                                                   |\n|  Guild card with picture of the Sun on it. I wonder why that person had     |\n|  it? London is a strange city. All that fog and everything...               |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Eternity Card      |  Slightly thicker. \"Eternity\" is written on it        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Eternity Card                                                              |\n|  Guild card acquired from a suspicious man. Makes one realize that just     |\n|  about anyone can be a guild member.                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Earth Gravestone   |  Stone with same wavelength as Earth Tombstone        |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Earth Gravestone                                                           |\n|  Oddly glowing stone. It gives off exactly the same wavelength as the one   |\n|  in the graveyard.                                                          |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|  Water Gravestone   |  Stone with same cold feeling as Water Tombstone      |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————————|\n|  Water Gravestone                                                           |\n|  Strangely glowing stone. It emits t